-- title:
--   Near orbits cannot touch the axis before crossing
-- statement:
--   Fix $0<\mu<1$ and a Jacobi energy $-c$ below the first critical value. Let $\Sigma_{\mu,c}$ be the selected Levi-Civita component and $\varphi$ a continuous flow on it generated by the Hamiltonian vector field of $K_{\mu,c}$. A state is $s=(z_1,z_2,w_1,w_2)$. Its physical position relative to the primary is $(x_1,x_2)=(2(z_1^2-z_2^2),\,4z_1z_2)$, and $(v_1,v_2)$ is its physical (Jacobi) velocity. A collision state has $z=0$. $N(r)$ and $F(r)$ are the perpendicular near and far starts at $z=(r,0)$ and $z=(0,r)$.
--
--   **Boundary exclusion (near side).** Let $s$ be a state with $z_2=w_1=0$, $z_1>0$ and $v_2(s)>0$, and let $T>0$. Suppose that for $-T<t<0$ the backward orbit satisfies
--   $$x_1(\varphi_ts)\ge0,\qquad x_2(\varphi_ts)\le0,\qquad z(\varphi_ts)\neq0.$$
--   Then one of two things happens. Either the orbit lies in the open quadrant $\{x_1>0,\ x_2<0\}$ for all $-T<t<0$, or $s$ already admits a near shooting arc of some length $\tau\in(0,T)$.
--
--   This upgrades the closed sign conditions obtained from a limit of near shooting arcs to the open ones. The mechanism is that a collision-free orbit cannot touch the axis $x_2=0$ from below while $v_1>0$: at such a contact $v_2=0$, and $\dot v_2=4|z|^2(2v_1+\Omega_y)>0$.
-- source:
--   Birkhoff 1915, The restricted problem of three bodies, §§16–18 (Collected Mathematical Papers Vol. 1, pp. 731–741); Liu–Salomão, arXiv 2506.17867v2, §5, pp. 30–31

import Definitions.Def_BirkhoffShootingArcs

namespace BirkhoffGlobalSection

theorem birkhoff_near_boundary_exclusion (μ c : ℝ)
    (hμ0 : 0 < μ) (hμ1 : μ < 1)
    (hc : belowFirstCriticalValue μ c)
    (φ : Flow ℝ (LeftEnergyState μ c))
    (hφ : IsLeviCivitaHamiltonianFlow μ c φ)
    (x : LeftEnergyState μ c) (T : ℝ) (hT : 0 < T)
    (hx1 : (x : Phase) 1 = 0) (hx2 : (x : Phase) 2 = 0) (hx0 : 0 < (x : Phase) 0)
    (hv : 0 < jacobiVelocity (leviCivitaToJacobi μ (x : Phase)) 1)
    (hcl : ∀ t ∈ Set.Ioo (-T) 0, 0 ≤ relativePosition μ ((φ t x : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase) 0 ∧ relativePosition μ ((φ t x : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase) 1 ≤ 0)
    (hP : ∀ t ∈ Set.Ioo (-T) 0, 0 < zNormSq ((φ t x : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase)) :
    (∀ t ∈ Set.Ioo (-T) 0, 0 < relativePosition μ ((φ t x : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase) 0 ∧ relativePosition μ ((φ t x : LeftEnergyState μ c) : Phase) 1 < 0) ∨
    ∃ τ : ℝ, 0 < τ ∧ τ < T ∧ IsNearShootingArc φ x τ := by sorry

end BirkhoffGlobalSection
